cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Profile-specific treatment effects from a nested trial, with and without dropout"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chang
    given-names: Evelyn
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Evelyn68961/nested-trial-cate-censoring"
abstract: >-
  A simulation study in R that rebuilds the estimator of Wen, Dahabreh and Chiu
  (Statistics in Medicine 2026) for conditional average treatment effects from a
  nested randomized trial, and extends it to time-to-event outcomes with dropout.
  The code, reports and lessons were written with an AI coding assistant (Claude Code).
keywords:
  - nested trial
  - conditional average treatment effect
  - dropout
  - inverse probability of censoring weighting
  - simulation study
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Generalizing Conditional Average Treatment Effects From Nested Randomized Trials to Trial-Eligible Individuals"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wen
      - family-names: Dahabreh
      - family-names: Chiu
    journal: "Statistics in Medicine"
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1002/sim.70767
